From 5bcef324c18500d0e7c0160117aa76527f11b7ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:48:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DHCP leases are kept across a restart (102.8 line)

- The lease lists live in RAM, so after a restart the router knew none of them: a device still
  holding a lease that did not ask again (a PC cabled to an AiMesh node) was missing from DHCP
  Leases and showed no name on Encrypted DNS until it renewed. The lease files of every network
  and the store of the names devices announce are now saved to the router's flash (when the set
  changes, hourly, and at reboot) and put back before each DHCP server starts on a fresh boot.
  This dnsmasq keeps the seconds left in its file, so no clock is needed; a malformed copy is
  refused.
- The name store no longer files a reserved device's reservation name as the name the device sent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
